# Day 03 - Linux Commands Practice

Today I practiced basic Linux commands on Playground platform.

## Commands I Learned

- pwd → shows current folder
- ls → shows files and folders
- cd → changes folder
- mkdir → creates new folder
- touch → creates new file
- cp → copies file
- mv → moves file
- rm → deletes file

## Process Commands

- ps → shows running processes
- top → shows system processes

## Networking Commands

- ping → checks internet connection
- ip addr → shows IP address
- curl → checks website response

## What I Learned

Today I learned how to use basic Linux commands for

- File management
- Process checking
- Network troubleshooting

This practice improved my Linux basics and terminal confidence.

